<!--
    GH-8017: "gcc -fstack-check stack-probing loop breaks rsp tracking"
    https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/8017

    gcc emits a stack-clash / -fstack-check probing loop for a large frame:

      lea    r11,[rsp-0x6000]     ; limit = SP_in + limit_const
    .L: sub    rsp,0x1000          ; probe step = one page
      or     QWORD PTR [rsp],0x0  ; touch the page
      cmp    rsp,r11
      jne    .L
      sub    rsp,0x40

    After heritage the loop-carried stack pointer is a spacebase MULTIEQUAL PHI
    whose back-edge is `PHI - 0x1000`; the StackSolver/spacebase tracker cannot
    break that self-referential cycle, so RSP never resolves to a constant past
    the loop.  Every post-loop local then renders relative to the loop
    induction variable as `&pxVar2[-0x1000]` page-probe noise:

      do {
        pxVar2 = pxVar1;
        *(undefined8 *)&pxVar2[-0x1000] = *(undefined8 *)&pxVar2[-0x1000];
        pxVar1 = &pxVar2[-0x1000];
      } while (&pxVar2[-0x1000] != axStack_6008);
      *(undefined8 *)&pxVar2[-0x1040] = ...

    Stage model: S2 stack-pointer normalization (spacebase tracking /
    ActionStackPtrFlow).  The kuna fix is a new simplification rule (group
    "analysis", gated by the default-off arch flag model_stack_probe_loop) that
    recognizes the probe loop (a 2-input spacebase MULTIEQUAL whose back-edge
    is `PHI - page` and whose loop-exit compares `PHI - page` against a
    stack-relative limit) and rewrites the MULTIEQUAL into the concrete
    `INT_ADD(SP_in, limit_const - page)`.  Breaking the cycle lets the spacebase
    tracker resolve the whole frame, eliminating the page-probe noise.
    Enabled by `option stackprobeloop on`.

    Pass 1 (default pipeline) reproduces the bug: the `&pxVar2[-0x1000]`
    page-probe noise survives (assert #1, exactly 3 noisy lines).
    Pass 2 (after `option stackprobeloop on`) resolves the stack PHI: NO
    `[-0x1000]` line remains, so over both passes the count is still exactly 3
    (assert #2: 3 in default + 0 in fix); were the fix to regress and leave any
    probe noise, the count would exceed 3 and assert #2 would fail.

    Disassembly (main, gcc -fstack-check, opt off):
      1149 push rbp / mov rbp,rsp
      114d lea  r11,[rsp-0x6000]
      1155 sub  rsp,0x1000
      115c or   QWORD PTR [rsp],0x0
      1161 cmp  rsp,r11
      1164 jne  1155
      1166 sub  rsp,0x40
      ... frame stores + two calls + ret
-->
